{"url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/46624731", "params": null, "fetched_at": "2026-11-24", "body": {"author": "arsentjev", "children": [{"author": "skeptrune", "children": [], "created_at": "2026-01-15T00:31:38.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768437098, "id": 46626171, "options": [], "parent_id": 46624731, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "Very cool!", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}, {"author": "xianshou", "children": [], "created_at": "2026-01-15T03:25:06.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768447506, "id": 46627635, "options": [], "parent_id": 46624731, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "Incidentally, Chroma also produced the single best study on long-context degradation that I&#x27;ve come across:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;research.trychroma.com&#x2F;context-rot\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;research.trychroma.com&#x2F;context-rot</a><p>Before that, I cited nolima (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.reddit.com&#x2F;r&#x2F;LocalLLaMA&#x2F;comments&#x2F;1io3hn2&#x2F;nolima_longcontext_evaluation_beyond_literal&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.reddit.com&#x2F;r&#x2F;LocalLLaMA&#x2F;comments&#x2F;1io3hn2&#x2F;nolima_...</a>) constantly to illustrate how difficult tasks involving reasoning or multi-step information gathering degraded much faster than the needle-in-haystack benchmarks cited by the major labs. Now Chroma is the first stop. Nice job on the research!", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}, {"author": "mappu", "children": [{"author": "pekim", "children": [], "created_at": "2026-01-15T15:52:44.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768492364, "id": 46634332, "options": [], "parent_id": 46628443, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "Looking at <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer&#x2F;blob&#x2F;master&#x2F;package.json\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer&#x2F;blob&#x2F;master&#x2F;pac...</a> it looks like it&#x27;s using Electron.", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}, {"author": "tonyplee", "children": [], "created_at": "2026-01-15T17:19:23.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768497563, "id": 46635874, "options": [], "parent_id": 46628443, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "files in <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer&#x2F;tree&#x2F;master&#x2F;src\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer&#x2F;tree&#x2F;master&#x2F;src</a> are .tsx (typescipt) code.", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}, {"author": "arsentjev", "children": [], "created_at": "2026-01-15T21:17:35.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768511855, "id": 46639453, "options": [], "parent_id": 46628443, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "it&#x27;s an Electron app that&#x27;s built to look like native. you&#x27;re right, the language is a bit misleading -- will update", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}], "created_at": "2026-01-15T05:31:23.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768455083, "id": 46628443, "options": [], "parent_id": 46624731, "points": null, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "Cool project!<p>I would hope &quot;native&quot; means at least either CPU-native code (i.e. not Typescript) or OS-native UI (i.e. not Electron) - what did you mean by it here?", "title": null, "type": "comment", "url": null}], "created_at": "2026-01-14T22:30:16.000Z", "created_at_i": 1768429816, "id": 46624731, "options": [], "parent_id": null, "points": 59, "story_id": 46624731, "text": "<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;stepandel&#x2F;chroma-explorer</a>", "title": "ChromaDB Explorer", "type": "story", "url": "https://www.chroma-explorer.com/"}}